Wait — actually there's a subtle detail: in the old code, `vprMachinePush = vprActorLogin === 'sm-silent-update'` — since the silent-update bot has NO login (noreply email, no account), the old backstop's committer check was dead code; the login check `vprActorLogin === vprMachineLogin` covered agent pushes. So a bot merge of main on a PR whose head it updated: old backstop — vprActorLogin = '' (bot merge has no login) → machinePushVf false → then vprFreshPush (bot merge date is fresh) → true → UNPARK! Wait — that means the OLD backstop would have UNPARKED on a bot merge (fail OPEN on bot merges)! The old backstop keyed committer check on login, which never matches → bot merge considered human → fresh date → cleared the park. Hmm, interesting: so the update_branch RESET (v2) held the park but the validate_pr backstop would have cleared it? Let me re-check the old v2 update_branch code:

Old update_branch:
```js
var lastCommitter = headCommitIdentity(...)  // committer NAME
var actorVf = headCommitActor(...)  // {login, date: .committer.date → ALWAYS ""}
var machinePushVf = lastCommitter === 'sm-silent-update' || (machineLogin && actorLogin === machineLogin);
var freshPushVf = !!(actorVf && actorVf.date && ...) // actorVf.date always "" → freshPushVf ALWAYS FALSE
```

Because of the `.committer.date` null bug, `freshPushVf` was ALWAYS false in production → the human-push RESET could NEVER fire at the update_branch site. And in the backstop: same `headCommitActor` (date always "") → `vprFreshPush` always false → backstop never cleared either. So the whole RESET was dead in production (the latent bug the PR says it fixed — "the freshness half of the RESET could never fire in production"). OK that matches the PR description.

Now with the fix: both sites can fire, and the walk makes them fire on the right commit. The new machinePushVf at the backstop now compares committer (correct identity) — good.

**Issue L — Consistency: the update_branch site checks `machinePushVf` BEFORE `freshPushVf`, backstop requires `vprFreshPush && !vprMachinePush`.** Equivalent logic (both require fresh && !machine). Fine.

**Issue M — one more subtle thing in the update_branch site:** the fail-closed branch condition changed from `lastCommitter === null || actorVf === null || parkedAtVf === null` to `actorVf === null || parkedAtVf === null`. Since lastCommitter is now derived from actorVf, equivalent. OK.

**Issue N — walk-per-tick cost:** each walk step = 1 gh api call. Two probe sites per parked PR per relevant rule. update_branch processes up to 20 (limit) BEHIND PRs; parked ones with bot merges walk 2 calls typically. Acceptable. SUGGESTION: could cap known by combining... not worth it.

