{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the machine-commit identity predicate now lives in 3 places**

The same test — `committer === 'sm-silent-update' || login === machineLogin` — is spelled out in:

1. `parkResetCommit`'s walk (this line),
2. `machinePushVf` in the `update_branch` RESET (~line 1293),
3. `vprMachinePush` in the `validate_pr` backstop (~line 1464).

That triplication is exactly how the drift this PR fixes was born: the backstop used to compare the **login** against `'sm-silent-update'` (a git committer *name* the bot has no login for — a dead check) while the RESET compared the **committer name**. Extract one helper, e.g.

```js
function machineCommitIdentity(commit, machineLogin) {
    var login = String((commit && commit.login) || '').toLowerCase();
    return String((commit && commit.committer) || '') === 'sm-silent-update' ||
        (!!machineLogin && !!login && login === String(machineLogin || '').toLowerCase());
}
```

(plus a `parents.length >= 2` variant for the merge-only walk), so the next identity change can't desynchronize the probes.
